				<td colspan="2"><img src="../images/insights/events.gif" alt="Events" width="602" height="79" border="0"></td>
			</tr>
			<tr valign="top">
				<td id="mainbody">
				
				<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" class="listtable">
					<tr valign="top">
						<td width="25%" nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">December 11, 2002</p></td>
						<td width="75%"><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Breaking the Language Barrier<br></span>
						<strong>Business Process Analysis to Object Oriented Analysis and Design</strong></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">See how your organization can break through the traditional language barrier that exists between business and IT. This 60-minute webinar will demonstrate the new link between Casewise Corporate Modeler and Rational RequisitePro and the proven approach that makes your business process analysis efforts seemlessly migrate directly into the software development process.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">November 26, 2002</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Universities as Catalysts for New Technology<br></span>
						<strong>Behind-the-Scenes Reports on Significant Technology in Chicagoland's Future</strong></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">You are encouraged to come to meet and hear thought leaders and visionaries from University of Chicago, University of Illinois, Loyola University, Northern Illinois University, Illinois Institute of Technology and Argonne National Laborotory who will share news and views about technology in the works.</p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Speakers from schools will present The Biggest and The Best development work underway at each institution, and also share at least one big technology success story per school. Representatives from the other two schools will serve as subject experts to facilitate audience questions and discussions.</p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">On the lookout for economic development opportunity for Chicagoland, this panel will tell us what's in the pipeline that we can identify and focus upon for further development, possible investment and other support.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">November 13, 2002</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Breaking the Language Barrier<br></span>
						<strong>Business Process Analysis to Object Oriented Analysis and Design</strong></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">See how your organization can break through the traditional language barrier that exists between business and IT. This 60-minute webinar will demonstrate the new link between Casewise Corporate Modeler and Rational RequisitePro and the proven approach that makes your business process analysis efforts seemlessly migrate directly into the software development process.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">October 29, 2002</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Women Leaders in Technology Speak Out</p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">What's right, what's wrong, and what needs to be thought of differently to help Chicagoland take center stage in today's quirky marketplace?</p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Women leaders in technology will bring us news, views and forecasts.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">September 24, 2002</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Proteomics and Allied Technologies<br></span>
						<strong>Is There Economic Promise for Chicagoland Inside the Human Proteome?</strong></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Top scientific, business, financial, academic and civic leaders will introduce the facts and the promise of Proteomics and allied technologies. Companies will be featured who focus serious research and development effort in this emerging field of scientific exploration. Do experts believe Chicagoland can capitalize on this opportunity?</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">July 30, 2002</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Biotechnology? Life Sciences? Science-Based Technology?</span></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Whatever "it" is called these days by investors and scientists, we'll take a good hard look at Biotech opportunity in Chicagoland's past, present and future.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">June 25, 2002</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Devils Disguised as Angel Investors?<br></span>
						<strong>The Devil is in the Details of Angel Investing for Technology</strong></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Why do so many angel investors tell high-tech applicants to go to...? ULCC Members and their Guests will hear and participate in an unguarded and unvarnished look at the gates to entrepreneurial heaven.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">May 21, 2002</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Nanotechnology - Thinking Big, Building Small</span></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Nanotechnology, or, as it is sometimes called, molecular manufacturing, is a branch of engineering that deals with the design and manufacture of extremely small electronic circuits and mechanical devices built at the molecular level of matter.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">April 30, 2002</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Biometrics - Jan Hertzberg, David Schwalb and Jeremy Appel - Axiom Security LLC</span></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Once a relatively obscure collection of disparate technologies, with steady yet unspectacular growth, Biometrics is now a robust growth industry. Fueled by increased public concern about security risks and greater social acceptance, Biometrics offer viable solutions to many of today's most perplexing security challenges.</p></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td colspan="2" class="grayrulebottom"><img src="../images/common/spacer.gif" alt="" width="420" height="9" border="0"></td>
					</tr>
					<tr valign="top">
						<td nowrap style="padding-top: 11px;"><p class="subhead2">February 28, 2002</p></td>
						<td><p class="bodycopysans"><span class="subhead1">Darcy Evons - Publisher of I-Street magazine</span></p>
						<p class="bodycopysmall">Darcy L. Evon started i-Street in January 1999 and launched the i-Street.com website, I-Street Reporter email newsletter community, and web broadcasts in March 1999. She secured funding for her venture from divine interVentures in November 1999. Darcy began a leading syndicated I-Street Internet column in the Chicago Sun Times in February 2000 and purchased the Chicago Software News magazine in April 2000. She most recently was the Vice President of Business Development at eBioSafe.com and previously the Vice President of Business Development for Veritel Corporation. She has held senior level positions in corporate development and technology transfer at Strategic Development Inc., the University of Chicago, and the University of Michigan Medical Center. While at the University of Chicago, she launched Chicago Connections, a newsletter for CEOs of Fortune 500 companies involved with the University.</p></td>
					</tr>
				</table>
				
